{"id": "EUVD-2026-76555", "enisaUuid": "fe71f5e4-72cb-3af8-a383-2e049b49dab2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\naudit: avoid dropping live tree ref on fsnotify rule autoremove\n\naudit_del_rule() is used for both netlink deletion templates and internal\nfsnotify autoremove.  The former passes a parsed template which owns a\ntemporary tree reference; the latter passes the installed entry itself.\n\nThe unconditional audit_put_tree() at the end of audit_del_rule() assumes\nthe template case.  For mixed AUDIT_DIR plus AUDIT_EXE rules, an fsnotify\nautoremove event therefore drops the installed rule's live tree reference.\nRepeating this across rules sharing the same tree can free the tree while\nanother rule still references it, and a later autoremove dereferences the\nfreed pathname while comparing rules.\n\nMove the temporary-tree put to audit_rule_change(), the caller that owns\ndeletion templates.  Keep it in the AUDIT_DEL_RULE cleanup so both\nsuccessful deletion and -ENOENT still release the parser-owned tree.\n\n[PM: dropped unnecessary comment for line length reasons]", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:45:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:50:15", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9cac21f8eb82675ed19fb955b8bbb9dd14cc3d58", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b322cc7adcd2e6ec1594d187533a126506ab545c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/695c85dc345a4e0292739f004c261bedef3f27e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01b0ec8c397be65ff710777c97017ca1de56ef8e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf37b61b5420fd4600fe78cf8c24da6e4d9bfe28", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/636a99bab36ba27515363d325866c0273ac83b3e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/583cf579b32d99e3fe4e9c8ecc4d852e3708fbec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/783f0f0974c156aca630f4ffff248671082a098d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qh9h-fg7c-vgxw", "CVE-2026-89643"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "096cce33-1f74-35e6-8eab-ab797b6090e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "1aef0d19-945b-35aa-866c-6e946edf88a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <783f0f0974c156aca630f4ffff248671082a098d"}, {"id": "3001a03d-e849-310a-8e5c-51b15f6d8879", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.3"}, {"id": "3101b2c5-0548-33c4-8ad8-f0c74b316d30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <01b0ec8c397be65ff710777c97017ca1de56ef8e"}, {"id": "34cb105c-3a81-323e-8d4e-b8c9a11f4f5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <9cac21f8eb82675ed19fb955b8bbb9dd14cc3d58"}, {"id": "45eb4bfc-f75f-3a54-92ba-f5d27285d32d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <636a99bab36ba27515363d325866c0273ac83b3e"}, {"id": "4788d6fc-b5ae-38be-b1a7-174ef35adf29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "660619b4-5c6e-3b9b-9b22-2ac1259746a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "67b9b86d-4447-3cd6-a3a5-25d25d234dd3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <cf37b61b5420fd4600fe78cf8c24da6e4d9bfe28"}, {"id": "810e6d84-de0d-3e1a-a8e9-73c78cde6a6e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "34d99af52ad40bd498ba66970579a5bc1fb1a3bc <583cf579b32d99e3fe4e9c8ecc4d852e3708fbec"}, {"id": "8bd066cb-6e99-3c87-99f3-f8e5168d5d32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Li